\f1\fs22 \'93You can add it to coffee if you don\'92t have a suitable mirror or other flat glassy surface,\'94 said Dr Nick.\
Nancy the housekeeper, who had been standing discreetly with a coffee service by the door, approached the bed, opened the tray\'92s legs and placed it over Sarah\'92s thighs. She poured coffee from a tall pot into a squat white cup, then lifted the creamer jug.\
\'93Black, please,\'94 Sarah said before Nancy could pour.\
Nancy stood back and chewed her disapproval. \'93You know it\'92s called half-and-half because it\'92s the other half of the coffee.\'94\
\'93Black,\'94 Sarah repeated.\
Nancy put the creamer down, reclaimed the coffee pot, and poured, as Dr John added a teaspoon of Dr Nick\'92s Mix and stirred.\
An hour later saw Sarah immersed in foundation-cracking music, dancing naked and jumping on the ornate bed. So vigorous and committed was her merriment, she neither noticed nor cared about shards of broadcast screen glass falling in her hair and onto the regal bed covers. As she danced, she salved her inferno-grade thirst from a briefcase-sized water bottle.\
The next morning, Sarah reflected on the nature of mortality as she pressed her forehead and nose against the grate of the shower drain, and hoped her stomach had done with turning itself inside-out for the day.\
A different Dr John arrived with a different Dr Nick. Like the former Dr John, he also prescribed Dr Nick\'92s Mix.\
\'93I have plenty of that, thank you,\'94 Sarah said while cradling her sore head. \'93Good day.\'94\
The next Dr John summoned by Nancy prescribed a peanut butter enema.\
After Nancy dispatched the latest of the Change of Habit Series, Sarah told her, \'93I want a real doctor.\'94
